"home" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		The Epic Elements
		<header>Every &lt;epic-*&gt; element an epic page is made of, how they nest, and a page for each.</>
	</>

	<list class="spell-meta">
		<item icon="user">Written for: anyone reading or writing an epic page's markup, or changing an element</>
		<item icon="flag">Status: <label size="mini" color="green">built</> every tag in <link title="epic/src/components/" target="src-spell-epic-src-components" link="/epic/src/components/"><text code>components/</></></>
		<item icon="book">The full markup rules: <link title="epic/src/tool/PLAN-DOC.md" target="src-spell-epic-src-tool-plan-doc-md" link="/epic/src/tool/PLAN-DOC.md"><text code>PLAN-DOC.md</></></>
	</>

	<section label="1. How they nest">
		<icon slot="icon" name="layer group"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Each tag is an element: it draws itself. <list bulleted><item>Its ATTRIBUTES are data (an item's <text code>status</>).</> <item>Its CHILDREN are prose (the doc's own words).</></></>
			<item>What it draws (chips, title lines, buttons, card headings) lives in its shadow root, never in the file.</>
			<item>Each is described once, in its vocabulary file (<text code>&lt;Name&gt;.en.ts</>): its attributes, their values, and which children it takes. <list bulleted><item>The browser and the epic tool both read it.</></></>
		</>
		<text paragraph>How the tags nest:</>
		<markdown>
			```text
			epic-page                    the whole doc:  header, crumbs, Send
			  epic-overview              the Overview
			    epic-summary             its two-sentence lede
			    epic-prompt              the kickoff prompt, folded
			    epic-section             one Overview part (kind="overview-part")
			  epic-section               phases, questions, judgements, todos, issues, manual tests, log
			    epic-phase               a phase
			      epic-field             Symptom, Changes, Goal, Done, Files, Verify ...
			      epic-update            a change to the phase's plan, after Goal
			      epic-commit            a commit
			    epic-item                a question, judgement call, todo, issue or manual test
			      epic-question          a question's text as first asked
			      prose elements         net effect, code, aside, note, labelled fields
			      epic-choices           option cards
			        epic-option          one option
			      epic-answer            the answer
			      epic-more              More Details
			      epic-reply             a reply card
			      epic-original          the Original Discussion
			        epic-version         one earlier version
			      epic-status            Claude's status card
			    epic-event               a log line (kind="log")
			```
		</>
		<text paragraph>Why it's built this way, and how a page draws: <link target="src-guides-epic-components-epic-components-html" link="/guides/epic-components/epic-components.html">Epic Pages as Components</>.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. The page and its sections">
		<icon slot="icon" name="map"/>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Tag</>
				<cell>Its role</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-page-html" link="/epic-page">
						<text code>epic-page</>
					</>
				</>
				<cell>The whole doc: holds its data (epic, title, branch, dates) and draws the header, crumbs, and Send.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-overview-html" link="/epic-overview">
						<text code>epic-overview</>
					</>
				</>
				<cell>The Overview: the summary, the kickoff prompt and the plan's prose parts, with the estimate total.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-summary-html" link="/epic-summary">
						<text code>epic-summary</>
					</>
				</>
				<cell>The Overview's two-sentence lede.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-prompt-html" link="/epic-prompt">
						<text code>epic-prompt</>
					</>
				</>
				<cell>The prompt that started the epic, as typed, folded under "Kickoff prompt".</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-section-html" link="/epic-section">
						<text code>epic-section</>
					</>
				</>
				<cell>One section by its <text code>kind</>: its numbered title, count and state filter; or an Overview part.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-phase-html" link="/epic-phase">
						<text code>epic-phase</>
					</>
				</>
				<cell>A phase: its status, estimate and fields.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-field-html" link="/epic-field">
						<text code>epic-field</>
					</>
				</>
				<cell>A labelled block: a phase's Symptom, Goal, Done ..., or "Where:" in an item.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-updated-html" link="/epic-updated">
						<text code>epic-updated</>
					</>
				</>
				<cell>RETIRED (2026-10-11): an older doc's change to a phase's plan, migrated to epic-update.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-update-html" link="/epic-update">
						<text code>epic-update</>
					</>
				</>
				<cell>An update: <text bold>Update</>: &lt;summary&gt; and its date, after what it changed (a phase's plan change, or prose); empty, the orange UPDATE label on an item changed while its phase runs.</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

