	<section label="6. Changing an element">
		<icon slot="icon" name="puzzle piece"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>A new one: <text code>spell pack add epics epic-&lt;name&gt;</>. Change the vocabulary first, then the class and its sheet.</>
			<item>Then <text code>yarn pack:build</> in the <link title="spell-epic" target="src-spell-epic" link="/spell-epic/">epics package</>, and commit its built pack (<link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-pack" link="/epic/src/components/__pack/"><text title="epic/src/components/__pack/" code>components/__pack/</></>) with the change. <list bulleted><item><text code>yarn test</> fails while the pack is stale.</></></>
			<item>Epic pages draw with <text code>main</>'s pack, so a change shows only once it merges. <list bulleted><item>Small fixes go straight on <text code>main</>.</></></>
			<item>A tag the docs already use, changed in its markup: a converter run, never a second way to read the old markup.</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>The rules in full: <link title="epic/src/AGENTS.md" target="src-spell-epic-src-agents-md" link="/epic/src/AGENTS.md">epics's <text code>AGENTS.md</></>.</>
	</>
